Such a simple but elegant solution.
Thank you, friend. Due to my still learning all of the ins and outs of MV's inner workings, that probably would have taken me an embarrassing amount of time to deduce on my own.
It works like a charm. Adding this line to Yanfly's plugin loads the spawned events into their initial spawn locations, just like I wanted. I had an issue where the move routes were still wonky due to the initial direction of the events not being retained. However, with further thought, I don't think I want the plugin to handle that.
In case anyone reading this later is curious, I remedied the direction issue by using Yanfly's Self Variables plugin, saved the initial direction I wanted the event to be facing when spawned to a Self Variable set on the freshly spawned event at creation, and added the following script call to the start of my template event's move route:
$gameMap.event(this._eventId).setDirection($gameSelfSwitches.value([$gameMap.mapId(), this.eventId(), 'SELF VARIABLE ' + 304]));
Click to expand...
In this example, "304" is my Self Variable ID.
Anyhow, my event works as intended, spawning in and moving along its intended route, even when leaving the map and returning. Thank you for saving me some headache, you've earned a spot in my credits roll.
